  "description": "PUWHAR crystallizes in the cubic crystal system with space group I -4 3 d. Reported CIF formula moiety: C76 H144 Dy4 Mn4 N8 O32,2(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Dy1MA (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy1Y (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy1N (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Mn1MA (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn1Y (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn1N (Mn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.377-3.957 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.58-116.38°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C76H144Dy4Mn4N8O32·2(C2H3N). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Mn(III), Dy(III).",
